    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "pack: a packing unit and measure for dry goods, flax, cloth, yarn, candlewick and similar wares — both a physical unit of transport of no particular size and, for some commodities, a measure of definite size (flax: 150 bales = 20 cwt at 112 lb./cwt; candlewick: 20 cwt; Irish yarn: 4 cwt at 120 lb./cwt; Cologne thread: 30 dozen lb.) (Zupko 270-1). See also packet, fardel, truss; for pack-thread see packthrede; for the pack-needle and packduck see those." ;
            crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 ] ;
